# Config/secrets layer captured nightly by backup-all.sh (same directory)
# (target "config"). One absolute path per line; blank lines and # comments are
# ignored. EVERY entry must be readable by the backup user or the target fails
# loudly. The archive is gpg-encrypted; nothing here is ever mirrored in plain.
#
# Why these: database dumps restore data, not the ability to start anything.
# These files hold the secrets and wiring that exist nowhere else (the override
# carries hardcoded secrets, .env files are gitignored, the four renders are
# produced from Doppler but pinned here so a Doppler outage cannot block a
# restore). The Langfuse env on dh40801 lives in Doppler project `langfuse`
# and is deliberately NOT here (there is no dh40801/.env).

